1
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:43,500
Get ready for a chilling fun holiday adventure with the Ice Age herd!

2
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Ice Age: A Mammoth Christmas is a animation, family, tv
movie film directed by Karen Disher.

3
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:58,500
When Sid accidentally destroys Manny's heirloom Christmas rock and ends up on Santa's naughty list, he leads a
hilarious quest to the North Pole to make things right and ends up making things much worse.

4
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Now it's up to Manny and his prehistoric posse to band
together and save Christmas for the entire world!

5
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:13,500
Manny (voice), played by Ray Romano.

6
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Sid (voice), played by John Leguizamo.

7
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:28,500
Ellie (voice), played by Queen Latifah.

8
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Diego (voice), played by Denis Leary.

9
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:43,500
Crash (voice), played by Seann William Scott.

10
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Eddie (voice), played by Josh Peck.

11
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:58,500
Ice Age: A Mammoth Christmas is a 2011 animated television special and part of the Ice
Age franchise, produced by Blue Sky Studios and directed by Karen Disher.

12
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:36,000
It premiered on November 24, 2011 on Fox in the United States and in the United Kingdom at
Christmas on Channel 4 and E4 and it was released 2 days later to DVD and Blu-ray.

13
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:13,500
This Christmas special takes place between Dawn of
the Dinosaurs and Continental Drift.

14
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Despite being produced by Blue Sky Studios, the film's animation was actually done by some animators at Blue Sky and
mainly by the Los Angeles/Dallas-based special effects and animation company, Reel FX Creative Studios.

15
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:28,500
The film explores themes of holiday, prehistory, christmas, short film.
